course: dictionary
lesson: 2333
title: Words for unkind acts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cruelty is behaviour that causes pain or suffering on purpose, or without caring. The clues are in the sentence: «Hurting animals on purpose is cruelty» tells you that the hurting is the cruelty, and the words on purpose show it is deliberate.
explain: A cruelty, with an a and an s at the end, means one cruel action. «Most Chinese today see it as a cruelty of the past» means that a cruel act from history is now seen as something wrong that belongs to the past.
explain: The sentences also show how people judge cruelty. «Animals can feel pain and fear, so most people believe ... that cruelty to animals is wrong.» Cruelty is wrong, and there are laws against it. If someone is cruel to you or to another person, tell a trusted adult.
fact: Cruelty means behaviour that causes pain or suffering on purpose, or without caring.
fact: A cruelty means one cruel action, so it has a plural: cruelties.
fact: Useful phrases are cruelty to animals, act of cruelty, and cruelty-free.
fact: Cruelty is a vice, a bad habit, and it is the opposite of kindness.
fact: Bullying is a kind of cruelty; tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Hurting animals on purpose is cruelty.» What does cruelty mean here? | Caring for animals every day | *Behaviour that causes pain on purpose | Being very quiet and shy | Running fast in the park
exercise: «Most Chinese today see foot binding as a cruelty of the past.» In this sentence, what does a cruelty mean? | *A cruel action | A happy memory | A kind rule | A type of animal
exercise: Which phrase means harming animals on purpose? | a good night's sleep | a happy pet | *cruelty to animals | kindness to animals
test: «Greed» and «cruelty» are bad habits. What is the word for a bad habit like these? | virtues | pains | laws | *vices
test: Someone is being cruel to you at school. What is the best thing to do? | Be cruel back to them | *Tell a trusted adult | Ignore it forever and hope it stops | Keep it secret and never say anything
exam: «Practise greed and cruelty and you grow greedy and cruel» suggests what happens when you repeatedly practise cruelty? | *You grow cruel | You grow taller | You forget how to read | You become a famous artist
